-- Every `NodeKind` and `TokenKind`, in declaration order, for the coverage
-- checks over the should_pass corpus.
--
-- Blorp has no enum reflection, so each kind names its successor in an
-- exhaustive `match`: adding a variant to either enum is a compile error here
-- until it is given an arm, and the inventory is the walk from the first kind
-- to the last, so there is no second list to keep equal to the enum. A variant
-- linked in at the wrong place is not caught by a count or an enum-source
-- comparison; the corpus coverage in `test_should_pass_coverage` fails when a
-- kind falls out of the walk, and review checks the order.
-- The tables' `node_schema` (when it is on main) maps each kind to its shape
-- but does not enumerate them, so it does not replace the chain; a test should
-- then check that `node_schema` covers every kind of `all_node_kinds()`.
import:
	../../../src/compiler_new/stage_01_discovery/tables/row_kinds:
		NodeKind(
			IdentifierNode,
			IntegerLiteralNode,
			FloatLiteralNode,
			StringLiteralNode,
			RawStringLiteralNode,
			PipeStringLiteralNode,
			RawPipeStringLiteralNode,
			InterpolatedStringNode,
			InterpolationTextNode,
			InterpolationHoleNode,
			InterpolatedPipeStringNode,
			TrueLiteralNode,
			FalseLiteralNode,
			CharLiteralNode,
			NegateNode,
			NotNode,
			DetachNode,
			AddNode,
			SubtractNode,
			MultiplyNode,
			DivideNode,
			ModuloNode,
			EqualNode,
			NotEqualNode,
			LessNode,
			LessEqualNode,
			GreaterNode,
			GreaterEqualNode,
			AndNode,
